{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Please do not leave us.</b> If I have not found favor in your eyes until now." "<b>For on this you know</b> our encampment — for on this account, that it was your intention to come with us, you know our camping." "<b>And you shall be for us as eyes.</b> Like 'if I have found favor in your eyes,' which is like 'before you' — so too here, from now on you shall be before us and with us as our eyes. Another interpretation: other converts will look at you and take heart to convert."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:21.199603442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}